1
00:00:00,087 --> 00:00:01,762
A thousand people move between

2
00:00:01,762 --> 00:00:03,175
two cities by the same

3
00:00:03,175 --> 00:00:04,750
rule every year.

4
00:00:04,750 --> 00:00:05,400
Where are they after

5
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:06,462
a hundred years?

6
00:00:07,067 --> 00:00:07,917
Each year,

7
00:00:07,917 --> 00:00:10,005
city one keeps eighty percent

8
00:00:10,005 --> 00:00:11,867
and sends twenty across;

9
00:00:11,867 --> 00:00:13,430
city two keeps seventy

10
00:00:13,430 --> 00:00:15,004
and sends thirty back.

11
00:00:15,004 --> 00:00:16,367
That's the matrix A.

12
00:00:16,942 --> 00:00:18,679
A turns most vectors:

13
00:00:18,679 --> 00:00:19,780
one thousand,

14
00:00:19,780 --> 00:00:21,580
zero becomes eight hundred,

15
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:22,380
two hundred.

16
00:00:22,992 --> 00:00:24,092
But six hundred,

17
00:00:24,092 --> 00:00:26,692
four hundred comes back unchanged:

18
00:00:26,692 --> 00:00:27,604
an eigenvector with

19
00:00:27,604 --> 00:00:28,605
eigenvalue one.

20
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:31,725
And anything along one, minus one,

21
00:00:32,138 --> 00:00:33,100
A just halves:

22
00:00:33,462 --> 00:00:35,050
eigenvalue one half.

23
00:00:35,667 --> 00:00:36,704
Split the start along

24
00:00:36,704 --> 00:00:39,205
the two lines: one thousand,

25
00:00:39,205 --> 00:00:41,667
zero is six hundred, four hundred,

26
00:00:41,667 --> 00:00:43,355
plus four hundred times one,

27
00:00:43,717 --> 00:00:44,429
minus one.

28
00:00:45,020 --> 00:00:46,745
Each year the green part stays

29
00:00:46,745 --> 00:00:48,208
and the red part halves:

30
00:00:48,571 --> 00:00:50,320
eight hundred, two hundred,

31
00:00:50,708 --> 00:00:51,983
right where A sent us.

32
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:54,587
Again it halves: one hundred,

33
00:00:54,587 --> 00:00:56,475
fifty, twenty-five,

34
00:00:56,475 --> 00:00:57,938
closing in on six hundred,

35
00:00:57,938 --> 00:00:58,750
four hundred.

36
00:00:59,333 --> 00:01:00,795
The start doesn't matter:

37
00:01:00,795 --> 00:01:02,045
every split of the thousand

38
00:01:02,045 --> 00:01:03,571
lies on the red line,

39
00:01:03,571 --> 00:01:04,371
and the whole line

40
00:01:04,371 --> 00:01:05,596
halves each year.

41
00:01:06,187 --> 00:01:07,038
A to the hundredth

42
00:01:07,038 --> 00:01:09,000
just powers the eigenvalues:

43
00:01:09,363 --> 00:01:11,400
one stays one, one half to the

44
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:13,637
hundredth is practically zero.

45
00:01:13,637 --> 00:01:15,350
Everyone ends at six hundred,

46
00:01:15,350 --> 00:01:16,262
four hundred.
